

A file system is the method an operating system uses to store, organize, retrieve, and manage files and directories on a storage device such as a hard disk, SSD, or USB drive.

File system → The catalog system that tells you where every book is located.

Without a file system, the operating system would not know where files are stored or how to retrieve them.




What does a file system do?
===========================
A file system is responsible for:

> Storing files on disk.
> Organizing files into directories.
> Managing file names and paths.
> Controlling permissions and ownership.
> Tracking free and used disk space.
> Retrieving files efficiently.
